      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(discord): bound stalled probe response reads",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Discord probe checks could hang after the `getMe` request returned response headers but the JSON response body stopped producing data.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Discord probe now reads the successful `getMe` JSON body through the bounded response reader with the existing 16 MiB cap and a per-chunk timeout tied to the probe timeout. Existing non-OK handling, malformed JSON wording, and probe result flow are preserved.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDiscord configuration checks now fail quickly on a stalled probe body instead of leaving users waiting on an unbounded read.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/discord/src/probe.intents.test.ts` (10 tests passed)\n- `git diff --check upstream/main..HEAD`\n- Claude autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings\n",
